_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 6
---
order: 6
---
short_label: X.6
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two magnitudes have to one another the ratio which a number has to a number, then the magnitudes are commensurable.
----
proof:

Let the two magnitudes {A|AA5} and {B} have to one another the ratio which the number {D} has to the number {E}.

I say that the magnitudes {A|AA5} and {B} are commensurable.

Divide {A|AA5} into as many equal parts as there are units in {D}, and let {C} equal one of them, and let {F} be made up of as many magnitudes equal to {C} as there are units in {E}.

