              highlighted: ["C","F","B"] },
            { text: "Further it measures {A|AA5} also, therefore {C} measures {A|AA5} and {B}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["C","AA5","B"] },
            { text: "Therefore {A|AA5} is commensurable with {B}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AA5","B"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "measured by the same measure C", ref: "X.Def.I.1" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if two magnitudes have to one another the ratio which a number has to a number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AA5","B","D","E"] },
            { text: "then the magnitudes are commensurable.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AA5","B","C"],
